```
Wait: with includeAdvisor and advisor findings filtered out by severity, goalMet still uses review.goalMet. If advisor had nit-only and reviewer says unmet → continue (reviewer). Fine.

If reviewer says met and advisor has concern → findings non-empty → continue, and `review.findings.length > 0` false but goalMet requires findings empty → false anyway. Good.

Edge: reviewer says met, advisor findings all below floor → findings empty, review.findings empty, goalMet true → converge. Good.

Reopen and `active.settled === "converged"`: if continue, new ledger without settled → reopens. If converged again → writes settled converged again. Fine.

But catch-up: reviewers should not be run when the last assistant is an old/a2... `pendingAdvisorFindings` uses scan.lastAssistant = last assistant index; late note after → found.

Need `allowReopen` also to bypass... no other guards.

Apply patch.

