Core tests pass. Now host tests: timers + advisor cases.

Patch double:
- add `timers` map and `runTimers`.
- change setTimeout/setInterval/clearTimer.
- expose runTimers.

Then tests.

Also `advisorNote` fixture in host test file.

Careful with plugin's `ctx.setInterval` returning handle: `state.refreshTimer`; clearTimer(0) etc. Use distinct ids in one map.

Implement:
```ts
const timers = new Map<number, () => unknown>();
let timerSeq = 0;
...
setTimeout(callback: () => unknown) { const id = ++timerSeq; timers.set(id, callback); return id; },
setInterval() { return 0; },
clearTimer(handle: number) { timers.delete(handle); },
```
But clearTimer receives ManagedTimer (any). Cast: `clearTimer(handle: unknown) { timers.delete(handle as number); }`.

`runTimers`: 
```ts
async runTimers() {
  const pending = [...timers.values()];
  timers.clear();
  await Promise.all(pending.map(cb => cb()));
}
```
`cb()` returns unknown; wrap `Promise.resolve(cb())`.

Type of `runTimers` in returned object.

Add tests:

A) advisor note alone:
```ts
it("drives a round from an unanswered advisor finding even when the reviewer accepts", async () => {
  const branch = [user("u1"), assistant("a1","done"), advisorNote("n1","missing test","concern")];
  ...
  host.queueReview(metReply());
  const result = await emit stop;
  expect(result.continue).toBe(true);
  expect(result.additionalContext).toContain("1. [concern] missing test");
  expect(host.appended...round 1
});
```
Wait: reviewer says met, advisor finding → union continue. Yes.

B) `/adversarial advisor off`:
```ts
arm; command "advisor off"; queueReview(metReply()); stop → undefined; ledger settled converged.
```
But config override set; `decideAtStop` includeAdvisor false → no advisor findings → converged.

C) stop signal: advisorNote with "[converged] ..." plus reviewer met → converged.

D) catch-up:
```ts
const branch = [user("u1"), ledger settled converged round 2, assistant("a2","done")];
host.arm; emit agent_start; emit agent_end;
branch.push(advisorNote("n2","late gap","concern"));
host.queueReview(unmetReply("late gap"));  // reviewer now sees the late note and agrees
await host.emit("message_end", { message: { role: "custom", customType: "advisor", content: "", details: { notes: [...] } } });
await host.runTimers();
expect(host.sent).toHaveLength(1); appended last round 3
```
Careful: the branch push must happen before message_end? The plugin re-reads branch in catch-up; push first.

Note `agent_end` sets endedAt; idle true.

Also `message_end` handler triggers only for custom/advisor.

Let's implement.

